    <h1>Nitro Coffee in Time of COVID-19 Pandemic How Safe is it</h1>
    <p class="muted">By John Goerke. <time datetime="2020-07-27">July 27, 2020</time> (updated <time datetime="2022-05-18">May 18, 2022</time>).</p>

    <p>This is a historical article, kept as originally framed. It is general information, not medical advice, and it has not been updated with new health claims; talk to a health professional about your own situation.</p>

    <p>This article was written during the COVID-19 pandemic, when many people asked how safe it was to have coffee prepared and served by someone else, and whether the way coffee is handled matters.</p>

    <h2>Hands-on coffee preparation</h2>
    <p>Traditional coffee service involves a lot of touching: cups, lids, equipment and hands. That raised questions about transmission at the time.</p>

    <h2>Handling and packaging</h2>
    <p>The article discusses how handling and packaging affect the service context, and how nitro coffee served on tap from a sealed keg differs from hands-on preparation. Learn more about <a href="/nitro-coffee-kegs/">nitro coffee kegs</a> and <a href="/nitro-cold-brew/">nitro cold brew</a>.</p>
  </article>
